ealth checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 18% across us-east, us-west, eu-west). Action taken: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all three production regions. Note: the rollback tool was persistently unavailable (503), so the rollback was performed via the deploy tool with v2.3.0 (a previously healthy production version, so no change-manager approval required). v2.3.1-rc (staging) was also unhealthy and was not considered. Follow-up needed: root-cause v2.3.1 before re-release and investigate the rollback tool outage.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 42818, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Ae5wDPZ8Z1dhHLvjNh4Y1r", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 42818, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Ae5wDPZ8Z1dhHLvjNh4Y1r", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 47455, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "Done. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Diagnosis**\n- checkout-api was running v2.3.1 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), unhealthy with an 18% error rate.\n- Release history showed v2.3.0 as the most recent release that was healthy in production. (v2.3.1-rc was staging-only and unhealthy, so it was excluded.)\n\n**Rollback**\n- The `rollback` tool was persistently unavailable (503 after multiple retries), so I performed the rollback via `deploy` of v2.3.0 instead. Since v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production, this did not require change-manager approval under policy.\n- v2.3.0 is now live in all three regions, and the service reports **healthy** with error rate down to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- Opened **INC-0001** (SEV2) for checkout-api; on-call has been paged. The summary documents the failure, the rollback to v2.3.0, the use of deploy as a workaround for the broken rollback tool, and follow-ups (root-cause v2.3.1 before re-release; investigate the rollback tool outage).", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by checking the current status and release history for checkout-api.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Rp9iQHSRk9bb8GzozbbyNT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01T9Da3CASqb1Lsy9CrcXcbb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01AyDPuv7MfPE9N65SqjYumG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01U7E6rmvuHDVBQG5tjkcxet", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "deploy", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "v2.3.0 is now rolled out to all three regions. Let me verify health and open the incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01HgBsBoUsAj37B3KdfeLpD1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Ae5wDPZ8Z1dhHLvjNh4Y1r", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 18% across us-east, us-west, eu-west). Action taken: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all three production regions. Note: the rollback tool was persistently unavailable (503), so the rollback was performed via the deploy tool with v2.3.0 (a previously healthy production version, so no change-manager approval required). v2.3.1-rc (staging) was also unhealthy and was not considered. Follow-up needed: root-cause v2.3.1 before re-release and investigate the rollback tool outage.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Done. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Diagnosis**\n- checkout-api was running v2.3.1 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), unhealthy with an 18% error rate.\n- Release history showed v2.3.0 as the most recent release that was healthy in production. (v2.3.1-rc was staging-only and unhealthy, so it was excluded.)\n\n**Rollback**\n- The `rollback` tool was persistently unavailable (503 after multiple retries), so I performed the rollback via `deploy` of v2.3.0 instead. Since v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production, this did not require change-manager approval under policy.\n- v2.3.0 is now live in all three regions, and the service reports **healthy** with error rate down to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- Opened **INC-0001** (SEV2) for checkout-api; on-call has been paged. The summary documents the failure, the rollback to v2.3.0, the use of deploy as a workaround for the broken rollback tool, and follow-ups (root-cause v2.3.1 before re-release; investigate the rollback tool outage).", "type": "text"}]}]}